Z||000008||Patrick's Dad||12-16-2001||09:11 PM||||Ray, never heard of Pacific.<P>Flatbeds simply run the lightwand over the transparency to a pickup. Still have problems with being perpendicular using nylon (plastic) gears and tracks. Especially having been shipped by UPS to a distribution center, then trucked to the locations....<P>True film scanners are the way to go, and stick with the names that know photography. I wouldn't buy an IBM or a Cisco car stereo, or a set of home speakers by HP. Wouldn't buy tires from them, either....<BR> <A HREF="http://www.how2scan.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.how2scan.com</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.nikonusa.com/usa_category/category.jsp?cat=7" TARGET=_blank>http://www.nikonusa.com/usa_category/category.jsp?cat=7</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fierokid87||12-16-2001||09:40 PM||||Flat beds are good if your just scanning pictures in for the heck of it or if your doing a web page.  <P>Scott<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="red"> Fierokid's  Web site:</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="white">http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero</FONT><P><FONT COLOR="blue">AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG">   <BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierokid-xmas-sig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||artherd||12-17-2001||01:18 AM||||You won't get a true 48bit path withought spending $10k+ for the sanner, then $40k on the (Silicon Graphics, no one else does it) computer, and another $100k on editing software...<P>Forget about the 'bit depth' stuff on consumer gear, they ALL output 24bit anyway.<BR>They simply use it as a BS marketing ploy.\<P>Avoid the flatbed, it will suck.<P>this is a good one:  <IMG SRC="http://www.nikonusa.com/images/products/9295_360.jpg"> <P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by ray b:<BR><B>comp USA add has a Prime film1800u by pacific image claims 1800 dpi 36 bit for 150<BR>but wife wants 48 bit rate<BR>anybody ever have a pacific unit????<BR>and is 48bitrate on a flatbed HP at 2400 dpi 48bit with active tranparency adapter [is that a small lite in the adapter?] is her pick so far.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
